+# YouTube Auto-Extraction Pipeline
+
+## Overview
+Automatically crawl YouTube channels/playlists, extract AI use cases using AI, and save them as drafts for admin review.
+
+## Architecture
+```
+YouTube API → Fetch Videos → Get Transcripts → AI Extraction → Save Drafts → Admin Review → Publish
+```
+
+## Environment Variables
+
+Add these to your `.env.local` and Vercel:
+
+```bash
+# YouTube Data API v3 (get from Google Cloud Console)
+YOUTUBE_API_KEY=your_youtube_api_key
+
+# OpenRouter API (for AI extraction)
+OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your_openrouter_api_key
+
+# Admin password (default: mateclaw2026)
+ADMIN_PASSWORD=mateclaw2026
+
+# Vercel Cron secret (auto-generated by Vercel, or set manually)
+CRON_SECRET=your_cron_secret
+
+# Telegram notifications (optional)
+TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your_bot_token
+TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=your_chat_id
+
+# App URL (for Telegram notification links)
+NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app
+```
+
+## Getting YouTube API Key
+1. Go to [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com)
+2. Create a project or select existing
+3. Enable "YouTube Data API v3"
+4. Create an API key under Credentials
+5. (Optional) Restrict the key to YouTube Data API v3
+
+## Adding YouTube Sources
+
+### Via Admin UI
+1. Go to `/admin/sources`
+2. Click "Add Source"
+3. Enter the channel/playlist details
+
+### Finding Channel/Playlist IDs
+
+**Channel ID:**
+- Go to the YouTube channel
+- View page source or use a channel ID finder tool
+- Format: `UC...` (starts with UC)
+
+**Playlist ID:**
+- Open the playlist on YouTube
+- Copy from URL: `youtube.com/playlist?list=PLxxxxxxx`
+- Format: `PL...` (starts with PL)
+
+### Popular AI Use Case Channels
+- **AI Jason**: `UCyR2Ct3pqOO7V4bLsqYk8AA` (AI tools & use cases)
+- **Matt Wolfe**: `UCMrXUsMBclkeTEB_9y3xSjw` (AI news & tools)
+- **All About AI**: `UC1GEbxXsX-1ZhHxVb8V8yWg` (AI tutorials)
+
+## Admin Dashboard
+
+### Access
+Navigate to `/admin` and enter the admin password.
+
+### Features
+1. **Dashboard** (`/admin`) - Stats overview + manual crawl trigger
+2. **Drafts** (`/admin/drafts`) - Review, edit, approve, publish, reject use cases
+3. **Sources** (`/admin/sources`) - Manage YouTube channels/playlists
+4. **Categories** (`/admin/categories`) - Manage and create categories
+
+### Draft Workflow
+```
+Draft → Approve → Publish
+  ↓
+Reject (with reason)
+```
+
+- **Publish**: Directly publishes the use case
+- **Approve**: Marks as approved (ready for batch publishing)
+- **Reject**: Marks as rejected with reason
+- **Edit**: Modify title, description, content, category, tags, difficulty
+
+### AI Confidence Score
+- **≥80%**: High confidence - clearly demonstrated in video
+- **50-80%**: Medium - mentioned but not fully shown
+- **<50%**: Low - tangential reference
+
+## Cron Job
+Configured via `vercel.json` to run every 12 hours:
+```json
+{
+  "crons": [{
+    "path": "/api/cron/youtube",
+    "schedule": "0 */12 * * *"
+  }]
+}
+```
+
+When new drafts are created, a Telegram notification is sent to the configured chat.
+
+## API Endpoints
+
+| Endpoint | Method | Auth | Description |
+|----------|--------|------|-------------|
+| `/api/pipeline/stats` | GET | None | Pipeline statistics |
+| `/api/pipeline/crawl` | POST | Admin | Trigger pipeline run |
+| `/api/admin/auth` | POST | None | Admin login |
+| `/api/admin/drafts` | GET | Admin | List drafts |
+| `/api/admin/drafts/[id]` | GET/PATCH/DELETE | Admin | CRUD single draft |
+| `/api/admin/sources` | GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE | Admin | CRUD sources |
+| `/api/admin/categories` | GET/POST/PATCH | Admin | CRUD categories |
+| `/api/cron/youtube` | GET | CRON_SECRET | Cron trigger |
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### "No transcript available"
+Some videos don't have captions. The pipeline will fall back to using the video description only, which may produce lower-quality extractions.
+
+### "YouTube API quota exceeded"
+The free tier allows 10,000 units/day. Each search request costs 100 units. Consider:
+- Reducing `maxResults` in fetchVideos
+- Using playlists instead of channels (cheaper API calls)
+- Requesting quota increase from Google
+
+### "OpenRouter API error"
+Check that your OPENROUTER_API_KEY is valid and has sufficient credits.
